-- Both one-sides carry two series per `host`, which the matching cannot resolve.
-- SQLNESS SORT_RESULT 3 1
TQL EVAL (0, 0, '1s') matching_groups_left{host="x"} / on(host) group_left matching_groups_right;

Error: 3001(EngineExecuteQuery), Execution error: found duplicate series for the match group {host="x"} on the right hand-side of the operation; many-to-many matching not allowed: matching labels must be unique on one side

